WEBVTT

00:01:28.325 --> 00:01:31.814
and whoever’s on it 
will fall into the ravine.

00:01:31.814 --> 00:01:33.452
Let’s look at an example.

00:01:33.452 --> 00:01:35.912
This stack would make itself stable.

00:01:35.912 --> 00:01:38.912
First the A blocks 
hold themselves in place.

00:01:38.912 --> 00:01:39.982
Then the B’s.

00:01:39.982 --> 00:01:43.672
And finally the C 
would nestle right between the B’s.

00:01:43.672 --> 00:01:47.122
However, suppose there was one more A.

00:01:47.122 --> 00:01:50.242
First two A blocks form up, then two B’s,

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:53.612
but now the remaining C and A 
have nowhere to go,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:56.072
so the whole thing falls apart.

00:01:56.072 --> 00:02:00.742
The Node of Power enables Hedge 
to energize a single stack of blocks.